OL,3,GNEWSAThe lifesaving decision that
OL,4,Auncovered my cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mother-of-five has said taking part
OL,7,Fin a research study for inflammatory
OL,8,Fbowel disease "saved her life" after a
OL,9,Fpreventive hysterectomy detected womb
OL,10,Fcancer.
OL,12,FAfter having her genes tested as part
OL,13,Fof a study in 2025, Victoria Thurston,
OL,14,F51, from Martlesham, Suffolk,
OL,15,Fdiscovered she had Lynch syndrome ` a
OL,16,Fgenetic condition making her
OL,17,Fpredisposed to cancer.
OL,19,FAfter deciding to have a hysterectomy
OL,20,Fto reduce the risk of cancer, during
OL,21,Fpreparation for surgery doctors found
OL,22,Fshe had early-stage womb cancer.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,374,370,200,160,0,100
